k of Warnaar. This k=1 cases turn out to be equivalent to identities of Jing, Misra, and Savage. Finally, we provide bijections for these identities involving two-rowed cylindric partitions, in the spirit of Corteel.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nau:Tang_F in:math - SciRate Search (https://scirate.com/search?q=au%3ATang_F+in%3Amath)\nciteturn1search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; @misc{2610.21702, author = {Fuying Tang and Shuo Shi}, title = {{A} proof of the interlacing conjecture for the singular values of {S}ylvester-{K}ac matrices}, year = {2026}, eprint = {2610.21702}, note = {arXiv:2610.21702v1} }[Button: Copy Citation] ... ~Wei}, title = {{A}n overpartition analogue of {B}ressoud conjecture for even moduli}, year = {2023}, eprint = {2312.00466}, note = {arXiv:2312.00466v1} }[Button: Copy Citation]\nWe first employ the bi-Hamiltonian structure of mCH to construct a novel hierarchy of explicit conservation laws with well-defined regularity domains. Then by formulating an appropriate Lyapunov functional, we apply the Inverse Scattering Transform to conduct a rigorous spectral analysis on the recursion operators. Finally, we demonstrate that the mCH $N$-solitons are non-isolated constrained minimizers of a variational problem. Our analysis proves that the $N$-soliton solutions of the mCH equation are both dynamically and orbitally stable in $H^{N+1}(\\mathbb{R})$. Notably, when reduced to the 2-soliton case, our framework establishes stability in $H^3(\\mathbb{R})$, which improves upon the existing regularity threshold.\n\n  * An overpartition analogue of Bressoud conjecture for even moduli\n\nY.H. Chen, T.T. Gu, Thomas Y. He, F. Tang, J.J. Wei\n\nDec 04 2023 math.CO arXiv:2312.00466v1\n\n[Button: Scited][Button: Scite!]\n\n0\n\n@misc{2312.00466, author = {Y.H.~Chen and T.T.~Gu and Thomas Y.~He and F.~Tang and J.J.~Wei}, title = {{A}n overpartition analogue of {B}ressoud conjecture for even moduli}, year = {2023}, eprint = {2312.00466}, note = {arXiv:2312.00466v1} }[Button: Copy Citation]\n\nPDF\n\nIn 1980, Bressoud conjectured a combinatorial identity $A_j=B_j$ for $j=0$ or $1$. In this paper, we introduce a new partition function $\\overline{B}_0$ which can be viewed as an overpartition analogue of the partition function $B_0$. An overpartition is a partition such that the last occurrence of a part can be overlined. We build a bijection to get a relationship between $\\overline{B}_0$ and $B_1$, based on which an overpartition analogue of Bressoud's conjecture for $j=0$ is obtained.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe Borwein conjecture and partitions with prescribed hook differences - MaRDI portal (https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/wiki/Publication%3A1918879)\nciteturn1search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 30.3 years ago; Crawled: 3 months ago;   * Extension of Bressoud's generalization of Borwein's conjecture and some exact results ...   * Bressoud's identities for even moduli. ... This page was last edited on 6 May 2026, at 22:18.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n(PDF) Combinatorial construction of Russell's series for partition classes defined by Capparelli, Meurman, Primc, and Primc in the $k$=1 Case (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/404836748_Combinatorial_construction_of_Russell%27s_series_for_partition_classes_defined_by_Capparelli_Meurman_Primc_and_Primc_in_the_k1_Case)\nciteturn1search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; Crawled: 5 months ago; The even moduli generalization of Theorem 3 is found by Bressoud [3]. ... in both Theorems 5 and 6 are either the series in Bressoud’s [4], the series in [13], or their\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nau:Jooken_J in:math - SciRate Search (https://scirate.com/search?q=au%3AJooken_J+in%3Amath)\nciteturn1search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; In t